    "extraction_notes": [
      "The datasheet contains usable digitizable plots on p. 2 and p. 3. Curve points are transcribed from the plotted traces without interpolation between unobserved points.",
      "Electrical characteristics table: hFE minimum 120 and maximum 400 at IC=50 mA, VCE=1.0 V; hFE minimum 40 at IC=500 mA, VCE=1.0 V; VCE(sat) maximum 0.6 V and VBE(sat) maximum 1.2 V at IC=500 mA, IB=50 mA.",
      "Small-signal table gives fT minimum 150 MHz at IC=20 mA and VCE=6 V, with measurement frequency f=30 MHz.",
      "Cobo and Cibo have no scalar electrical-characteristics table entries; their available information is provided as digitized Fig.6 curves at f=1 MHz and Ta=25 degC, so the scalar fields are null.",
      "Maximum ratings include VCBO=40 V, VCEO=25 V, VEBO=5.0 V, IC=0.5 A, and collector power dissipation PC=300 mW at Ta=25 degC.",
      "Electrical-characteristics breakdown minima are V(BR)CBO=40 V at IC=100 uA, IE=0; V(BR)CEO=25 V at IC=0.1 mA, IB=0; and V(BR)EBO=5.0 V at IE=100 uA, IC=0.",
      "Electrical-characteristics leakage maxima are ICEO=0.1 uA at VCE=20 V, IB=0; ICBO=0.1 uA at VCB=40 V, IE=0; and IEBO=0.1 uA at VEB=5.0 V, IC=0.",
      "The plotted static characteristic has Ta=25 degC and base-current traces from IB=50 uA through 400 uA. The plotted gain, saturation, base-emitter-on, and capacitance curves are separately labelled with their temperatures or test frequency as recorded in each curve entry.",
      "The hFE classification table gives rank ranges L=120-200, H=200-350, and J=300-400."
    ],
